## Review Checklist

### Server-First Architecture (CRITICAL)

- [ ] Pages are async Server Components (no `'use client'`)
- [ ] Data fetching in `src/lib/data/` (server-only, `cache()` wrapper), awaited by the page
- [ ] Mutations in `src/lib/actions/` with `'use server'`
- [ ] `revalidatePath()` called after mutations
- [ ] Client Components only for interactivity (buttons, forms, filters, modals) and get data as props
- [ ] No `useEffect` fetching of a page's own data; client fetching only for client-driven data
- [ ] `params` / `searchParams` typed as `Promise<...>` and awaited (sync access removed in Next.js 16)
- [ ] Server-only modules (`src/lib/data`, `src/services`) never imported from `'use client'` files
{% if variables.i18n %}

### Internationalization ({{ variables.i18n }})

- [ ] Pages live under `src/app/[locale]/` and call `setRequestLocale(locale)`
- [ ] No hardcoded user-facing strings: copy via `getTranslations` / `useTranslations`
- [ ] New message keys exist in every `src/messages/*.json` ({{ variables.locale_count }} locales)
- [ ] Links/redirects use the locale-aware helpers (`@/i18n/navigation`) where needed
- [ ] No hardcoded locale lists — derive from `src/i18n/config.ts`
{% endif %}

### TypeScript

- [ ] No `any` types (use `unknown` with type guards)
- [ ] `type` used for props (not `interface`)
- [ ] All functions have proper return types
- [ ] No `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`
- [ ] No non-null assertions (`!`)

### React/Next.js

- [ ] `'use client'` only where necessary
- [ ] Uses {{ variables.ui_library }} components where appropriate
- [ ] `@/` imports used (not relative imports for internal)
- [ ] Named exports (except pages)
- [ ] `notFound()` for missing resources
- [ ] `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx` where appropriate

### Performance

- [ ] No unnecessary Client Components
- [ ] `useCallback` for handlers passed to children
- [ ] `useMemo` for expensive computations
- [ ] Proper key props in lists
- [ ] Images use Next.js `<Image>`

### Server Actions (BLOCKING if missing)

Every Server Action is a public POST endpoint, callable with any arguments.

- [ ] **Authenticates** inside the action (session checked in the action itself, not only in the page/UI/`proxy.ts`)
- [ ] **Authorizes** the specific resource (queries scoped by owner/tenant/role; a forged ID cannot touch other users' data)
- [ ] **Validates** every argument with Zod (`safeParse`), including IDs and `FormData`
- [ ] Field errors via `z.flattenError(error)` (Zod 4; `error.flatten()` is deprecated)
- [ ] Form actions have the `(prevState, formData)` signature used by `useActionState`
- [ ] `revalidatePath()` / `revalidateTag()` after data mutations
- [ ] `redirect()` for navigation after success, called outside `try/catch`
- [ ] Error handling with typed response; no internal details or secrets returned
- [ ] Truly public actions (contact, sign-up) are rate-limited

## Verdict Format

Return ONE of:

### APPROVED
```markdown
## Review: APPROVED

All checks passed.

### Strengths
- <what was done well>
```

### NEEDS_CHANGES
```markdown
## Review: NEEDS_CHANGES

### Required Changes

1. **[file.tsx:42]** <issue>
   - Problem: <what's wrong>
   - Fix: <how to fix>
```

### BLOCKED
```markdown
## Review: BLOCKED

### Blocking Issues

1. **<issue>**
   - Problem: <security/architectural concern>
   - Required: <what needs to change>
```

## Common Issues

### Client-Side Data Fetching (WRONG)
```typescript
// BAD - useEffect for data fetching
'use client';
useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api/projects').then(res => res.json()).then(setProjects);
}, []);

// GOOD - Server Component
export default async function Page() {
  const projects = await getProjects();
  return <ProjectList projects={projects} />;
}
```

### Unnecessary 'use client'
```typescript
// BAD - Client Component just to display data
'use client';
export function ProjectCard({ project }: Props) {
  return <Card>{project.name}</Card>;
}

// GOOD - Server Component (no directive)
export function ProjectCard({ project }: Props) {
  return <Card>{project.name}</Card>;
}
```

### Server Action Without Auth (BLOCKED)
```typescript
// BAD - anyone can POST this action with any id
'use server';
export async function deleteProject(id: string) {
  await db.project.delete({ where: { id } });
}

// GOOD - authenticate, validate, authorize (owner-scoped)
'use server';
export async function deleteProject(projectId: string) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  const id = z.string().uuid().parse(projectId);
  const { count } = await db.project.deleteMany({ where: { id, ownerId: user.id } });
  if (count === 0) throw new Error('Not found');
  revalidatePath('/projects');
}
```

### Sync params (Next.js 16 error)
```typescript
// BAD
export default async function Page({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {
  const project = await getProject(params.id);
}

// GOOD
export default async function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ id: string }> }) {
  const { id } = await params;
  const project = await getProject(id);
}
```

### Missing Server Action
```typescript
// BAD - API route for mutation
// app/api/projects/route.ts
export async function POST(request: Request) { ... }

// GOOD - Server Action
// lib/actions/projects.ts
'use server';
export async function createProject(prevState: State, formData: FormData) { ... }
```

### Missing revalidatePath
```typescript
// BAD - No cache invalidation
export async function deleteProject(projectId: string) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  await db.project.deleteMany({ where: { id: projectId, ownerId: user.id } });
  // Missing revalidatePath!
}

// GOOD
export async function deleteProject(projectId: string) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  await db.project.deleteMany({ where: { id: projectId, ownerId: user.id } });
  revalidatePath('/projects');
}
```
